<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear list for Feral Druid DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic for Phase 3. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from Heroics, reputation rewards, and the new 10-man Raid loot added to Titan Rune Dungeons.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot-gear">Feral Druid DPS Best in Slot Gear, Gems, and Enchants - Pre-Raid Phase 3</h2>When planning out your character's pre-raid gearing in WotLK Classic, the first thing to note is that itemization for Ferals has been greatly simplified in WotLK compared to vanilla and TBC. All leather DPS gear now follows a simple formula of providing two primary attributes, Agility and Stamina, and 2-3 secondary stats at fixed ratios relative to the amount of Agility on the item. As a result, the total allocation of useful stats on any gear piece is entirely determined by its item level, and a new piece of gear with higher item level than your current piece will almost always be a DPS upgrade, regardless of the details of what stats are present on the two items. This means that, especially early on in your character's gear progression when you are flooded with gear options from dungeons, professions, reputation rewards, and other sources, you really do not need to think too hard about what pieces to equip, and can use item level as an excellent proxy for DPS when evaluating potential upgrades. The highest item level that is attainable in most gear slots prior to entering a 10-man or 25-man raid in Phase 3 is 225 or 239, and unsurprisingly, the embedded pre-raid BiS setup below uses a 225 or 239 item level piece in the majority of slots.<br/>
<br/>Given the dominance of item level as the most important attribute for gearing, the only change to pre-raid stat priorities for Feral DPS in Phase 3 relative to prior phases is that Armor Penetration and Agility become relatively more efficient stats compared to Attack Power and Strength. This is due to two key rotational changes arising from the new <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=413895/glyph-of-omen-of-clarity">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Omen of Clarity</span></a> interaction that was recently implemented by Blizzard:<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=413895/glyph-of-omen-of-clarity">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Omen of Clarity</span></a> effectively results in an additional <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48572/shred">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_vampiricaura.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shred</span></a> cast every 6 seconds via the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=16870/clearcasting">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_manaburn.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Clearcasting</span></a> procs generated from casting <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=16857/faerie-fire-feral">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_faeriefire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Faerie Fire (Feral)</span></a> on cooldown. As a result, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48572/shred">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_vampiricaura.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shred</span></a> will now contribute a larger fraction of your total DPS output than in prior phases, making Armor Penetration (which buffs <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48572/shred">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_vampiricaura.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shred</span></a> damage but not bleed damage) a more valuable stat than previously.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">The massive Energy savings induced by <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=413895/glyph-of-omen-of-clarity">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Omen of Clarity</span></a> mean that it is no longer efficient to frequently "bearweave" in order to fill empty GCDs with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=9634/dire-bear-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_racial_bearform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dire Bear Form</span></a> casts, as doing so usually results in either Energy capping or delaying a <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=16857/faerie-fire-feral">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_faeriefire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Faerie Fire (Feral)</span></a> cast. Strength was previously a more efficient DPS stat than Agility in bearweaving rotations, since Agility does not provide any Attack Power when in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=9634/dire-bear-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_racial_bearform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dire Bear Form</span></a>, but this is now reversed since you will be spending almost all of your DPS time in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=768/cat-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_catform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cat Form</span></a>.</div></li></ol>In practice, the only consequence of these stat weight changes is that <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40117/fractured-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Cardinal Ruby</span></a> becomes your new default gem of choice even at pre-raid gear levels.<br/>
<br/>Shown below is a recommended gear configuration that can be easily assembled by a Feral Druid in Phase 3 prior to entering any WotLK raids. The set includes only items that can be farmed in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/news/wotlk-classic-ptr-3-4-2-sidereal-essence-glyph-of-shattering-throw-titan-rune-332917">Titan Rune Beta</a> dungeons (either directly from boss drops or indirectly via <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=221/emblem-of-conquest">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_championsgrace.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Conquest</span></span></a> and <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=2589/sidereal-essence">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_icediamond_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sidereal Essence</span></span></a> accumulation), and omits PvP rewards or expensive BoE items:<br/>
<div style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
